    "title": "Man injured after shooting on Mariners Way in Norfolk - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Valenti Govantes ,\n6 hours ago NORFOLK, Va. (WAVY) -- A man was injured after a shooting on Mariners Way Wednesday afternoon, according to the Norfolk Police Department.\nThe shooting happened at a home in the 500 block of Mariners Way at around 4:25 p.m. on Aug. 26.\nWAVY Photo Officers were originally dispatched to Fire Station 7 for a reported gunshot victim who had arrived at the station. The man was taken to a local hospital with non-life-threatening injuries.\nThis is an ongoing investigation.\nIf you have any information about this case, you can submit an anonymous tip by calling 1-888-LOCK-U-UP, downloading the P3 tips app to a mobile device, or visiting www.P3tips.com and submitting a tip.\nCopyright 2026 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed.\nFor the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to WAVY.com.\n1",
